comment.narrative:
Target exceeded. 
- Fully functional 66% and partially functional 34%. 
- 450 FVCC actively engaged in preventing IUU fishing; 
- Raising awareness on marine fisheries laws and improved community compliance; 
- Maintaining fish sanctuaries, aiding in marine biodiversity conservation. 
- VFCC meeting-7942, UFCC meeting-256 and DFCC meeting-21

Target exceeded. 
- 231,432 fishers HH members (53,790 Fishers/Fishers Households Mobilized` in 450 villages, 4.3 persons per household in the rural area); 
- 68,000 fishers (8,500 Artisanal vessels with GSM, about 8 fishers per vessel on average); 
- Cluster farmers HH members 31,927 (4.3 person per HH); 
- 150 (5 Industrial Trawler with V-SAT MTU, about 30 crews per trawler).

- 53,790 Fishers/Fishers Households Mobilized in 450 villages, of which 97% female; 
- Training 11,262 community leaders, of which 8,624 females, led to effective implementation of the Fisheries Management Development Plan; 
- Vocational and skill development training to 16,913, of which 6,627 females; - Vulnerable identified 1,863, 100% female.
